INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(76,'population-vs-sample',62,0,'FAIL: (1) worked ex step 4 says 3 of 8 study >8h but data 5,7,6,9,8,7,10,6 has 2 (p-hat 0.25 not 0.375; propagates to Figure, step 5, mistakes bullet); (2) only 4 question-phrased core H2s, template needs 5-8; (3) Census PEP claim ''administrative records and sample-based survey data'' not on cited page (it says births/deaths/migration) and ''roughly 330 million'' unsourced; (4) Penn State STAT200 1.1 source redirects to course home /stat200/ (title mismatch). WARN: 1 worked example vs plan''s 5; PSU/prc232/eda352 sources not cited inline; ''about 6%'' is 6.5%.','2026-10-04 18:13:14');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(77,'population-vs-sample',92,1,'Round 2: all R1 fixes verified (8+ hrs count=3, 5 question H2s, Census para matches PEP page, Yale replaces Penn State, 6.5% and biased division shown); 8/8 links 200, titles match, quotes verbatim, arithmetic recomputed, no cannibalization','2026-10-04 18:18:06');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(78,'descriptive-vs-inferential-statistics',64,0,'HARD: (1) worked example sum of squared deviations is 874.1 not 873.1, so s2=97.12 and s=9.86 (not 97.01/9.85); (2) standard error defined as ''SD of a statistic divided by sqrt(n)'' is wrong, should say SE of the mean = s/sqrt(n) (SE is itself the SD of the sampling distribution); (3) CDC NHIS and Census ACS about pages do not state the sampling-error / margin-of-error claims they are cited for, so cite pages that do. WARN: research/business H2 not question-phrased; 7 sources (<8); CLT cited for SE shrinkage, which comes from Var(xbar)=sigma2/n','2026-10-05 01:23:12');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(79,'descriptive-vs-inferential-statistics',88,1,'Round 2 PASS: all 6 round-1 fixes verified; arithmetic recomputed (SS=874.10, s=9.86, SE=3.12, CI 72.64-86.76, t=1.51); 8/8 sources 2xx with claims confirmed (CDC NHIS methods, ACS handbook ch1); keywords owned; overlap 0 FAIL 0 WARN. WARNs: CDC href 301-redirects to /nchs/nhis/about/nhis-methods.html; worked example does not state the 10 students were randomly sampled.','2026-10-05 01:29:55');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(80,'descriptive-vs-inferential-statistics',65,0,'Build gate FAIL at draft:false: check-links found 2 violations -> /calculators/mean-median-mode-range/ missing (calculator is standalone:false, no page). Fix lines 205 and 223: replace routes.calculator(''mean-median-mode-range'') with routes.article(''mean-median-mode-range'') and adjust anchor text (e.g. ''mean, median, mode, and range guide and calculator''). All content checks otherwise pass (arithmetic, 8/8 sources, keywords, overlap 0/0). WARN: CDC href 301s to /nchs/nhis/about/nhis-methods.html; worked example does not say the 10 students were randomly sampled.','2026-10-05 01:31:13');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(81,'descriptive-vs-inferential-statistics',68,0,'1) HARD worked-example rounding: line 170 ''2.262 x 3.12 ~= 7.05'' is false (=7.057 -> 7.06), so shown work gives CI (72.64, 86.76) not (72.65, 86.75). Fix: carry s ~= 9.855 into SE = 9.855/sqrt10 ~= 3.116, MoE = 2.262 x 3.116 ~= 7.05, CI (72.65, 86.75), t = 4.7/3.116 ~= 1.51 (lines 160,168,170,177); or keep 3.12 and use 7.06 / (72.64, 86.76) in lines 170,171,182. 2) WARN: line 141 implies ~30 students per section with n=10 sampled (n/N ~ 1/3) and no finite population correction; state the population as the course/process or note the FPC. 3) WARN: FAQ 2 generalizes one class to ''every student who will ever take that exam'', which contradicts the article''s random-sample rule; reword as a random sample of exam-takers. All else passed: gate 18/18, 8 sources 200 with matching titles, quotes verbatim, SS=874.1, s=9.86, Var(xbar)=sigma^2/n, keywords owned, overlap 0 FAIL/0 WARN.','2026-10-05 16:55:10');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(82,'descriptive-vs-inferential-statistics',90,1,'Round 2: MoE 2.262x3.12=7.06 and CI (72.64, 86.76) consistent; population now ~240-student course cohort (FPC 0.98, negligible); FAQ 2 states random sample of exam-takers. Gate 18/18, overlap 0/0, 8 sources live, quotes verbatim.','2026-10-05 16:56:17');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(83,'sampling-methods',66,0,'HARD: (1) NIST prc232 mis-cited - it is chi-square sample sizes for variance tests, not margin-of-error sizing; replace with prc222 (7.2.2.2, error-of-estimation sample size) and fix Sources entry. (2) Worked example step 5 states +/-7.2 pp MOE with no shown arithmetic; add fenced calc. WARN: NCES source not cited inline; no per-method pros/cons table; 5,000 vs 4,850 population/frame wording muddled.','2026-10-06 01:38:05');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(84,'sampling-methods',90,1,'Round 2: all 6 fixes verified. NIST prc222 supports error-of-estimation sizing; MOE arithmetic shown and correct (0.072); NCES design-effect + NHANES (Series 2 No.162) quotes verbatim; 9/9 links 200; sanitizer 18/18; overlap 0/0; keywords owned.','2026-10-06 01:44:15');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(85,'sampling-methods',90,0,'Content PASS (90) but publish build gate failed, unrelated to article: check-docs - docs/status/sessions/2026-09-06-adsense-audit.md and 2026-09-06-agentic-workflow-restructure.md older than 30 days and outside archive/. Reverted to draft: true. Archive those two docs, then re-run the publish; no rewrite needed.','2026-10-06 01:45:26');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(86,'sampling-methods',66,0,'Round 3 (rewritten draft). HARD: (1) Yale multistage claim misattributed - Yale says ''more practical ... for on-location analysis such as door-to-door surveys'', never mentions avoiding a master list; reword to Yale''s claim or cite StatCan 3.2.2 (which says no list of all students needed). (2) ''What Are the Pros and Cons...'' H2 opens with the DataTable, no direct-answer sentence. (3) Tip Callout ''single most common error in intro statistics courses'' is an unsourced superlative; soften to ''a common confusion''. WARN: StatCan 3.2.1 and Census ACS Sources not linked inline; tools CTA says ''turn the formulas above into a number'' but no sample-size formula is shown. Passed: sanitizer 18/18, overlap 0/0, keywords owned, 8/8 links 200 + titles match, all quotes verbatim, arithmetic correct.','2026-10-06 06:59:00');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(87,'sampling-methods',68,0,'Round 2/2 (capped): 1) HARD misattribution in Multistage bullet: article says StatCan 3.2.2 two-stage design means ''you would not need to have a list of all Grade 11 students'' (only class lists + student lists); the source says that of its THREE-stage design (400 schools x 2 classes x 10 students); its two-stage design explicitly requires a list of all Grade 11 students in the selected schools. Change ''a two-stage design'' to ''a three-stage design (schools, then classes, then students)''. 2) WARN: ACS sentence claims the page''s figures ''only mean something because selection probabilities are known''; the page reports sample size/coverage/response/item-allocation rates and never mentions margin of error or selection probabilities - reword to what the page shows. All else passes: sanitized 18/18, 8/8 sources 200 + titles match, all quotes verbatim, arithmetic correct, keywords owned, overlap 0 FAIL 0 WARN.','2026-10-06 07:05:53');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(88,'independent-vs-dependent-variables',64,0,'HARD: (1) mis-citation ''Concepts in Biology'' vs page title ''Concepts of Biology''; (2) OpenStax bio example is a phosphate/algae control-ponds (control group) experiment, not a ''pond-fertilizer'' one and not a control-variable definition; (3) worked example calls 8->14->11 ''diminishing returns'' (it is an optimum/decline), no closing decision, and a misleading linear-regression ''check the arithmetic'' link; (4) unsourced empirical claims in answer para (''single most common reason'') and checklist framing (''catch nearly every mix-up'', ''where most people guess wrong''). WARN: 7 sources (<8) and 1.1 Definitions source not cited inline/does not mention IV/DV; extraneous-variable definition uncited; description says ''10 worked examples'' (they are practice examples).','2026-10-07 01:29:08');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(89,'independent-vs-dependent-variables',88,1,'R2 PASS: sanitizer 18/0, overlap 0/0, 8/8 sources 200 + titles match, quotes verbatim, arithmetic ok, all 8 R1 fixes verified. WARNs: sentence 1 frames rather than defines; OpenStax 1.1 variable definition loosely paraphrased','2026-10-07 01:37:14');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(90,'sampling-methods',62,0,'1) StatCan 3.2.2 Ex.6 misread: ''would not need a list of all Grade 11 students'' is StatCan''s multistage-vs-SRS benefit, not ''only 3-stage avoids a list'' - rewrite multistage para 2 + Common Mistakes bullet 2 + worked-ex step 1 aside; 2) ACS sentence overstated: S9801 page lists unit response, coverage, item response (not allocation), combined rates and CV - no sample size; 3) Yale multistage ''since it concentrates data collection...'' clause not in Yale - end at quote or attribute to StatCan; 4) Pew ''with a stated margin of error'' not on cited page; 5) worked-ex step 4 ''120'' unjustified - show a design-effect calc or label as assumption, soften step 5 MOE claim; fix N clash (N=14,000 vs N=68 -> n); 6) unsourced: SRS ''least bias of any method'' (prose+table), multistage Pro tip ''one-stage cluster ... more precise''','2026-10-07 14:02:32');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(91,'sampling-methods',68,0,'R2: 1 HARD - line 99 misdescribes StatCan Example 6 as a district survey across 100 schools (''district''s full enrollment'', ''district-wide'' appended to verbatim quote); StatCan''s example is national (Canada) and its two-stage design selects ''more schools'' than 100. WARNs: PMC snowball sentence (''2017 study recruiting'' + unsourced ''since...initial contacts and venues'' clause); Pro tip drops StatCan''s ''in most cases'' hedge for cluster; ''Real large-scale surveys usually combine more than one technique'' unsupported by the Pew/ACS examples. Round-1 fixes 1-7 otherwise verified.','2026-10-07 14:10:04');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(92,'sampling-methods',92,1,'Round 3 confirmation: all 4 round-2 fixes verified verbatim against StatCan/PMC; all 8 sources 200 with matching titles; math recomputed (67.77->68); keywords owned; overlap 0/0. WARN: worked-example step 4 drops the ''usually'' hedge for cluster designs (multistage claim itself is supported).','2026-10-07 14:12:24');
